Comments:
    Identical to helical-MHDTurb, except that io_hdf5 is used (and we use mpicomm since nompicomm does not work with hdf5_io_parallel).
    The purpose is to test whether the Python routines in pc.read work with HDF5 simulations.
    
    I have also removed the lzero_spec_zerok to get the sample to work on my somewhat older development branch.
    
    For unknown reasons, the 2D averages (yaver and zaver) do not match those in the helical-MHDTurb sample. The current reference data are the same as in the standard (nohdf5, nompicomm) sample, and thus this test currently fails (running script tests).
    Note that the output for io_dist+mpicomm are the same as io_dist+nompicomm, so it looks like the introduction of HDF5 is somehow changing the results (but only of the 2D (yaver, zaver) averages).
